1
00:00:20,450 --> 00:00:22,910
Can a Boy-Girl Friendship Survive?

2
00:00:21,330 --> 00:00:22,910
(No, It Can't!!)

3
00:01:30,520 --> 00:01:34,440
The Meaning Behind Sunflowers

4
00:01:35,640 --> 00:01:37,500
Memories of summer...

5
00:01:37,710 --> 00:01:40,200
<i>What?! Go head-to-head?</i>

6
00:01:40,630 --> 00:01:44,330
Sounds like this only got out of hand 
because of Onii-chan!

7
00:01:44,760 --> 00:01:47,040
I won't deny that.

8
00:01:47,360 --> 00:01:50,580
There's no way Yu can win 
if he's getting judged by Kureha-san!

9
00:01:50,580 --> 00:01:55,260
I'll just decline her offer, 
and you can pay off my debt!

10
00:01:56,360 --> 00:02:00,920
We're only in this mess because 
you lied about going to Tokyo.

11
00:02:00,920 --> 00:02:02,580
<i>You're</i> liable for this!

12
00:02:02,580 --> 00:02:04,640
The Inuzuka Family won't get involved!

13
00:02:04,640 --> 00:02:07,900
Come on! Have a heart!

14
00:02:07,900 --> 00:02:11,760
I still can't believe she 
wants Yu-kun to pay this off.

15
00:02:11,760 --> 00:02:14,480
She's rotten to the core.

16
00:02:14,480 --> 00:02:17,900
Next time she's home, I'll take her to Mom 
if I have to drag her myself.

17
00:02:18,270 --> 00:02:22,940
Kureha will resort to anything 
if it means meeting her goal.

18
00:02:23,750 --> 00:02:27,380
She channeled all her negative energy 
into getting to the top, after all.

19
00:02:27,770 --> 00:02:28,960
Negative energy?

20
00:02:29,610 --> 00:02:31,260
Like when people make fun of her.

21
00:02:31,260 --> 00:02:33,280
It just fuels her fire.

22
00:02:33,440 --> 00:02:34,870
She's the opposite of you.

23
00:02:34,870 --> 00:02:35,990
Y-Yeah.

24
00:02:36,240 --> 00:02:38,960
You work hard for people who support you.

25
00:02:39,540 --> 00:02:43,170
To her, you guys aren't passionate enough.

26
00:02:43,720 --> 00:02:46,100
Not that there's a right or wrong.

27
00:02:46,100 --> 00:02:47,800
Then what if I ran away?

28
00:02:48,490 --> 00:02:51,520
Knowing Kureha, she'll stick to the rules.

29
00:02:51,980 --> 00:02:54,880
But I imagine she'll at least 
open her own store next to yours.

30
00:02:54,880 --> 00:02:58,990
Then invest a bunch of money 
to put you out of business.

31
00:02:59,280 --> 00:03:01,100
That's not even funny.

32
00:03:03,440 --> 00:03:05,610
Yu-kun, no need to worry.

33
00:03:06,200 --> 00:03:08,990
If you lose, feel free to hand Himari over.

34
00:03:08,990 --> 00:03:11,340
That way, you can open your store with me!

35
00:03:11,760 --> 00:03:15,070
Thanks, I'll make sure not to lose then!

36
00:03:15,970 --> 00:03:19,620
Anyways, just do your best as usual.

37
00:03:19,900 --> 00:03:24,100
Remember, I'm here because I fell 
for your accessories.

38
00:03:24,100 --> 00:03:25,560
Y-Yeah.

39
00:03:25,760 --> 00:03:29,070
Either way, I have to win 
for Himari to stay.

40
00:03:30,110 --> 00:03:32,320
<i>That's right. I have no time to waste.</i>

41
00:03:33,150 --> 00:03:36,410
<i>I've been spoiled by the people 
around me for too long.</i>

42
00:03:37,020 --> 00:03:39,270
<i>My work has to attract 
people who don't know me.</i>

43
00:03:40,410 --> 00:03:43,830
<i>Like Saku-nee-san said, 
I can't stay frozen in time!</i>

44
00:03:47,400 --> 00:03:50,410
There he is. Yu!

45
00:03:52,410 --> 00:03:55,130
Come on, let's go look for summer memories!

46
00:03:56,240 --> 00:04:00,640
That sounded so cheesy. 
Even I feel embarrassed.

47
00:04:00,640 --> 00:04:02,800
Well it's summer break.

48
00:04:02,800 --> 00:04:05,090
This is the cheesiest time of our lives!

49
00:04:05,280 --> 00:04:09,600
Don't forget, you're 
the one who's on the line here.

50
00:04:10,430 --> 00:04:12,410
It's fine, I know you'll win!

51
00:04:12,410 --> 00:04:14,330
And I have a backup plan just in case.

52
00:04:14,330 --> 00:04:15,270
Backup plan?

53
00:04:17,150 --> 00:04:19,230
I'll join their agency then quit right away!

54
00:04:19,230 --> 00:04:23,140
You know, that's how you 
always set people off.

55
00:04:23,140 --> 00:04:25,870
Besides, that means you'd 
have to drop out of school.

56
00:04:26,400 --> 00:04:27,670
Like that's a problem?

57
00:04:27,670 --> 00:04:29,740
You'd take care of me for life, right?

58
00:04:29,740 --> 00:04:33,140
D-Don't phrase it like that! 
It's misleading.

59
00:04:33,140 --> 00:04:35,450
We'll be co-owners. Okay?

60
00:04:35,800 --> 00:04:38,200
Phrase it like what?

61
00:04:38,200 --> 00:04:40,510
Well, I mean... it sounds like...

62
00:04:40,510 --> 00:04:42,420
Marriage, you know?

63
00:04:42,620 --> 00:04:43,200
Huh?

64
00:04:46,370 --> 00:04:50,480
When have I ever said 
that I <i>don't</i> mean it like that?

65
00:04:52,190 --> 00:04:54,640
You promised to only have eyes 
for me, remember?

66
00:04:57,380 --> 00:05:00,270
Himari, I promise 
to win against Kureha-san—

67
00:05:04,240 --> 00:05:06,190
Bwa-ha!

68
00:05:06,190 --> 00:05:07,960
It's been a while since I got you!

69
00:05:07,960 --> 00:05:09,700
Himari!

70
00:05:11,660 --> 00:05:14,090
You've been kinda cold recently.

71
00:05:14,090 --> 00:05:16,040
Make me "Bwa-ha!" some more.

72
00:05:16,040 --> 00:05:17,920
What kind of a request is that?

73
00:05:18,990 --> 00:05:20,790
Yu-kun, Hii-chan.

74
00:05:21,960 --> 00:05:23,530
Hey, Enocchi!

75
00:05:23,530 --> 00:05:25,260
I was just saying how Yu's been cold.

76
00:05:25,260 --> 00:05:26,930
Comfort me!

77
00:05:26,930 --> 00:05:29,640
I bet you probably said something rude.

78
00:05:30,380 --> 00:05:33,800
<i>Man, her distrust in Himari is palpable.</i>

79
00:05:34,640 --> 00:05:38,090
Yu-kun, let's go look for summer memories.

80
00:05:38,810 --> 00:05:39,600
See ya!

81
00:05:39,600 --> 00:05:40,460
Take care!

82
00:05:47,260 --> 00:05:50,060
Maybe you should be more 
mindful of what you eat.

83
00:05:50,240 --> 00:05:52,780
It could affect your performance.

84
00:05:54,800 --> 00:05:56,330
Is that supposed to be advice?

85
00:05:56,330 --> 00:05:58,380
Everyone has their own pace.

86
00:05:58,570 --> 00:06:01,500
I'm only working at the best pace for me.

87
00:06:01,700 --> 00:06:03,820
That's certainly impressive.

88
00:06:04,340 --> 00:06:08,590
Speaking of which, looks like 
Kureha-kun got you off your game.

89
00:06:08,920 --> 00:06:11,760
Let me guess. You offered 
to help and she declined?

90
00:06:14,400 --> 00:06:15,660
Nice theory.

91
00:06:15,920 --> 00:06:19,800
But I'd say you're the one getting played.

92
00:06:20,130 --> 00:06:22,730
Let's see... She tried 
to blackmail you with a video?

93
00:06:23,500 --> 00:06:27,700
I'd prefer to think of it as 
providing her with entertainment.

94
00:06:27,910 --> 00:06:30,810
You came all the way here 
to keep me in check,

95
00:06:30,810 --> 00:06:33,440
but I'm afraid it won't work on me.

96
00:06:33,920 --> 00:06:36,280
I support Natsu and his work.

97
00:06:36,280 --> 00:06:38,760
But not as much as I support Rin-chan.

98
00:06:39,180 --> 00:06:41,350
Keep you in check? Of course not.

99
00:06:41,760 --> 00:06:45,540
As long as Yu-kun can 
pour his all into his work,

100
00:06:45,540 --> 00:06:46,660
that's all that matters.

101
00:06:48,550 --> 00:06:52,720
You focus on tennis, and don't 
worry about anything else.

102
00:06:55,720 --> 00:06:56,130
So?

103
00:06:56,450 --> 00:06:58,480
Did you come up with any summer memories?

104
00:07:00,280 --> 00:07:01,350
Nope.

105
00:07:01,730 --> 00:07:03,000
It's such a common theme.

106
00:07:03,000 --> 00:07:04,480
And way too broad.

107
00:07:04,940 --> 00:07:08,440
Not to mention, I can't get 
on the same page with this "client."

108
00:07:08,640 --> 00:07:10,940
Try starting with scenery then!

109
00:07:11,160 --> 00:07:13,700
Why not take a bunch of pictures

110
00:07:13,700 --> 00:07:15,580
then try to match that with a flower later?

111
00:07:16,030 --> 00:07:19,480
So the opposite of when 
Enomoto-san first modeled for us?

112
00:07:19,790 --> 00:07:21,820
I'm not very good at that, though.

113
00:07:22,730 --> 00:07:26,300
How about Enocchi 
and I come up with some ideas?

114
00:07:26,760 --> 00:07:29,830
Hii-chan, you can only come up 
with raunchy stuff.

115
00:07:29,830 --> 00:07:31,130
No way!

116
00:07:31,130 --> 00:07:33,550
I'm a high school girl, you know!

117
00:07:33,940 --> 00:07:36,140
You don't usually act like it.

118
00:07:36,690 --> 00:07:38,520
Do you have any ideas?

119
00:07:45,800 --> 00:07:46,640
It's dusk.

120
00:07:47,400 --> 00:07:50,450
I'm a guy walking home after club practice.

121
00:07:50,900 --> 00:07:54,660
Together with my childhood friend.

122
00:07:54,960 --> 00:07:56,970
Oh, you're storytelling?

123
00:07:57,890 --> 00:07:59,500
Suddenly, rain starts falling.

124
00:08:00,280 --> 00:08:02,600
We find shelter, but we're soaking wet.

125
00:08:03,280 --> 00:08:05,360
I look at her sheer—

126
00:08:05,360 --> 00:08:06,110
Sheer?

127
00:08:07,140 --> 00:08:10,350
Her sheer shirt and pink bra!

128
00:08:10,350 --> 00:08:11,950
I couldn't help myself but—

129
00:08:11,950 --> 00:08:12,840
Scratch that idea.

130
00:08:13,270 --> 00:08:14,590
No raunchy stuff allowed!

131
00:08:14,850 --> 00:08:18,250
I don't wanna be Hii-chan's 
number one, after all.

132
00:08:18,440 --> 00:08:19,720
Don't be so rude.

133
00:08:19,720 --> 00:08:21,750
What about you then, Enocchi?

134
00:08:21,750 --> 00:08:23,430
You've always liked girly manga.

135
00:08:23,430 --> 00:08:26,320
I'm sure you have a scenario in mind!

136
00:08:26,980 --> 00:08:30,640
Well... I'm not picky or anything.

137
00:08:31,350 --> 00:08:33,560
Anywhere's fine if it's with Yu-kun.

138
00:08:33,560 --> 00:08:36,400
No one's talking 
about their ideal first time!

139
00:08:37,210 --> 00:08:39,340
Enocchi, you dirty girl!

140
00:08:38,570 --> 00:08:40,550
Himari, no teasing!

141
00:08:41,250 --> 00:08:42,630
But we're talking about her first time.

142
00:08:42,630 --> 00:08:44,330
I'm good anywhere.

143
00:08:44,330 --> 00:08:46,910
W-Well so am I.

144
00:08:45,110 --> 00:08:47,870
<i>I guess we'll start with obvious ideas.</i>

145
00:08:46,910 --> 00:08:48,370
Then we're both good.

146
00:09:03,440 --> 00:09:04,800
Take this, Enocchi!

147
00:09:05,210 --> 00:09:06,930
Hii-chan, that was cold!

148
00:09:12,400 --> 00:09:13,350
They look the part.

149
00:09:13,680 --> 00:09:14,520
How was that?

150
00:09:14,960 --> 00:09:17,200
I got a few good shots.

151
00:09:17,200 --> 00:09:19,780
Did you have to splash me that much?

152
00:09:20,150 --> 00:09:21,630
My bad.

153
00:09:21,630 --> 00:09:25,040
You can stop by my place 
and I'll take it out for cleaning.

154
00:09:25,290 --> 00:09:27,750
But your clothes won't fit me.

155
00:09:28,090 --> 00:09:30,840
Are you dissing the size of my boobs?

156
00:09:30,840 --> 00:09:32,160
Well played, Enocchi.

157
00:09:32,160 --> 00:09:33,680
Well it's the truth.

158
00:09:34,220 --> 00:09:36,550
Why I oughta!

159
00:09:35,950 --> 00:09:38,080
Wanna piece of me?

160
00:09:39,430 --> 00:09:41,150
I sure do!

161
00:09:41,150 --> 00:09:43,720
Wait, don't Hii-chan!

162
00:09:43,720 --> 00:09:46,300
Ah, to be young and wild.

163
00:09:54,490 --> 00:09:56,760
It's cute, don't you think?

164
00:09:57,360 --> 00:09:59,400
Yeah, I like it.

165
00:09:59,840 --> 00:10:02,840
I mean, it definitely feels like summer.

166
00:10:03,070 --> 00:10:05,120
But it's almost like an ad.

167
00:10:05,440 --> 00:10:10,460
Not that it's bad, but I'm not 
sure it goes with the theme.

168
00:10:11,920 --> 00:10:14,100
How much time do we have left? Three weeks?

169
00:10:14,570 --> 00:10:15,240
Yeah.

170
00:10:16,230 --> 00:10:17,900
This is a lot harder than I thought.

171
00:10:18,280 --> 00:10:21,400
It's like I'm thinking too hard about it.

172
00:10:21,400 --> 00:10:23,590
Hey, come on! Not fair!

173
00:10:24,710 --> 00:10:25,440
Take that!

174
00:10:28,890 --> 00:10:29,820
Something wrong?

175
00:10:30,400 --> 00:10:31,190
Nothing.

176
00:10:31,580 --> 00:10:35,490
Hey, there's somewhere I wanna visit.

177
00:10:41,820 --> 00:10:42,880
This is it?

178
00:10:43,270 --> 00:10:45,730
It's a flower arranging 
school I used to go to.

179
00:10:46,160 --> 00:10:48,320
It's been a while since my last visit.

180
00:10:51,370 --> 00:10:53,590
Take this! Special dive attack!

181
00:10:53,590 --> 00:10:55,180
No fair, Sensei!

182
00:10:54,220 --> 00:10:55,480
She's the teacher?

183
00:10:55,480 --> 00:10:56,360
Grow up!

184
00:10:55,690 --> 00:10:57,040
That's her.

185
00:10:57,500 --> 00:10:59,040
Oh, hi there.

186
00:11:01,860 --> 00:11:04,160
I see you still like gaming.

187
00:11:04,160 --> 00:11:05,220
I do!

188
00:11:05,410 --> 00:11:10,180
I've been hooked since 
I started back when you were here.

189
00:11:11,520 --> 00:11:13,350
What can I help you with today?

190
00:11:14,160 --> 00:11:18,730
I was hoping you could 
show me other people's work.

191
00:11:20,160 --> 00:11:21,110
Wow, Natsume-kun.

192
00:11:21,110 --> 00:11:23,480
That's a surprising request coming from you.

193
00:11:23,720 --> 00:11:25,920
It's a long story.

194
00:11:27,110 --> 00:11:28,790
Hey! Look!

195
00:11:29,030 --> 00:11:30,350
Is this Hii-chan?

196
00:11:30,350 --> 00:11:33,340
Yup. I used to come here for a bit, too.

197
00:11:33,520 --> 00:11:37,440
Your work is meh, 
but you were cute back then.

198
00:11:38,400 --> 00:11:40,300
You say that like I'm not cute now.

199
00:11:40,510 --> 00:11:42,760
You're not growing your hair out anymore?

200
00:11:44,450 --> 00:11:46,280
It's a shame, it's so pretty.

201
00:11:46,510 --> 00:11:50,430
But can't be helped if Natsume-kun 
likes Inuzuka-chan's hair short.

202
00:11:51,690 --> 00:11:53,200
Yu, is that true?

203
00:11:53,400 --> 00:11:55,210
I-I meant it generally.

204
00:11:55,210 --> 00:11:58,360
I think the general consensus is 
that you look good with short hair.

205
00:11:58,810 --> 00:12:01,120
But that's subjective!

206
00:12:01,120 --> 00:12:03,250
So basically, you totally love me.

207
00:12:03,250 --> 00:12:05,600
You're head-over-heels 
in love with me, right?

208
00:12:05,600 --> 00:12:06,080
I'll go short.

209
00:12:06,080 --> 00:12:07,630
No, it's fine!

210
00:12:07,630 --> 00:12:09,000
You have pretty hair!

211
00:12:09,000 --> 00:12:10,530
I think your hair looks great!

212
00:12:12,080 --> 00:12:16,410
Since you're all here, wanna 
make some flower arrangements?

213
00:12:16,940 --> 00:12:17,920
You wouldn't mind?

214
00:12:19,200 --> 00:12:22,160
I'm sure you'll get more inspired 
working with your own hands.

215
00:12:22,470 --> 00:12:24,130
Wanna give it a shot, Enomoto-chan?

216
00:12:24,480 --> 00:12:26,600
Yes, I'd love to.

217
00:12:26,980 --> 00:12:27,970
What about you?

218
00:12:27,970 --> 00:12:31,440
Oh, um... I'll just watch!

219
00:12:36,100 --> 00:12:40,560
<i>Ever since I was little, 
I've sucked at making stuff.</i>

220
00:12:41,730 --> 00:12:43,760
<i>Generally, I'm good at everything.</i>

221
00:12:44,160 --> 00:12:46,560
<i>As long as I know all the right steps,</i>

222
00:12:46,560 --> 00:12:49,970
<i>I'm pretty good at following 
instructions. But...</i>

223
00:12:51,240 --> 00:12:53,910
<i>I'm not good at making things creatively.</i>

224
00:12:54,320 --> 00:12:57,630
<i>Art, cooking, flower arrangements...</i>

225
00:12:57,860 --> 00:13:00,130
Yu-kun, this is pretty hard.

226
00:13:01,600 --> 00:13:03,800
<i>Man, it's like a pork katsu bowl.</i>

227
00:13:04,650 --> 00:13:07,990
<i>See, it's hard to make 
things off the script.</i>

228
00:13:08,450 --> 00:13:11,180
<i>If Enocchi was good on her first try,</i>

229
00:13:11,180 --> 00:13:13,040
<i>how sad would I look?</i>

230
00:13:13,800 --> 00:13:15,270
Oh, then try this.

231
00:13:15,560 --> 00:13:18,210
Think of one side while 
you're getting the hang of it.

232
00:13:18,540 --> 00:13:21,730
Don't worry about the back, 
and use fewer flowers.

233
00:13:22,790 --> 00:13:24,980
Okay. Let me try.

234
00:13:29,850 --> 00:13:30,840
<i>That's beautiful.</i>

235
00:13:31,710 --> 00:13:33,060
What do you think?

236
00:13:33,460 --> 00:13:36,070
Looks great. Much better than the first try.

237
00:13:41,800 --> 00:13:43,600
<i>It's a shame, it's so pretty.</i>

238
00:13:44,250 --> 00:13:45,750
<i>Back in middle school,</i>

239
00:13:46,070 --> 00:13:48,260
<i>I once jumped onto Yu while he was working,</i>

240
00:13:48,260 --> 00:13:49,680
<i>and accidentally burned my hair.</i>

241
00:13:50,090 --> 00:13:53,490
<i>I felt so bad seeing Yu apologize.</i>

242
00:13:54,280 --> 00:13:57,190
<i>I cut it all off when 
we entered high school.</i>

243
00:13:57,660 --> 00:13:59,000
No, it's fine!

244
00:13:59,000 --> 00:14:00,400
You have pretty hair!

245
00:14:00,400 --> 00:14:01,950
I think your hair looks great!

246
00:14:02,370 --> 00:14:03,300
<i>Hey, Yu?</i>

247
00:14:03,750 --> 00:14:05,800
<i>What if I had long hair, too?</i>

248
00:14:06,130 --> 00:14:08,960
<i>What if I were feminine 
and girly, like Enocchi?</i>

249
00:14:10,290 --> 00:14:11,920
<i>Would you have eyes only for me?</i>

250
00:14:20,170 --> 00:14:21,970
That girl, Enomoto-chan.

251
00:14:21,970 --> 00:14:23,330
She's the hibiscus girl, isn't she?

252
00:14:23,740 --> 00:14:25,550
Sensei, you can tell?

253
00:14:29,520 --> 00:14:31,940
She likes Natsume-kun too, huh?

254
00:14:31,940 --> 00:14:36,040
Yup, she's committed. 
She's liked him for seven years.

255
00:14:36,050 --> 00:14:37,050
How about Natsume-kun?

256
00:14:37,320 --> 00:14:40,770
He says he doesn't, but I know he likes her.

257
00:14:42,040 --> 00:14:43,500
That's youth for ya!

258
00:14:43,500 --> 00:14:45,400
Keep your cool, Inuzuka-chan.

259
00:14:46,750 --> 00:14:49,110
What do you mean? I'm always cool.

260
00:14:49,480 --> 00:14:50,500
Are you?

261
00:14:50,500 --> 00:14:53,700
You suddenly went from 
having zero romantic feelings

262
00:14:53,700 --> 00:14:57,700
to becoming cling—I mean, 
a girl with a crush!

263
00:14:57,700 --> 00:14:59,780
N-No, I'm not!

264
00:14:59,780 --> 00:15:02,090
Himari, for the battle with Kureha-san,

265
00:15:02,320 --> 00:15:04,160
I think I'll do a piece on sunflowers.

266
00:15:07,840 --> 00:15:10,560
It's the one from your 
exhibit in middle school.

267
00:15:10,880 --> 00:15:14,510
<i>The sunflower wreath Yu made me.</i>

268
00:15:15,520 --> 00:15:17,560
It can stand its own against Kureha-san.

269
00:15:17,560 --> 00:15:18,890
It'd be perfect.

270
00:15:20,080 --> 00:15:21,850
I think that's a great idea!

271
00:15:22,560 --> 00:15:25,840
Enomoto-san actually picked this out.

272
00:15:27,440 --> 00:15:28,560
Oh, cool.

273
00:15:28,840 --> 00:15:31,320
I know where you can find sunflowers!

274
00:15:31,320 --> 00:15:34,280
Sunflower Festival

275
00:15:37,640 --> 00:15:39,700
Sucks Enocchi couldn't come.

276
00:15:40,040 --> 00:15:43,590
It can't be helped, 
she has to help out at the store.

277
00:15:44,430 --> 00:15:46,150
Why are you sitting behind me?

278
00:15:46,150 --> 00:15:47,360
Let's sit together.

279
00:15:47,360 --> 00:15:48,800
Oh, um...

280
00:15:48,980 --> 00:15:51,220
Oh yeah, I have to eat breakfast.

281
00:15:51,920 --> 00:15:52,800
I forgot my drink.

282
00:15:53,110 --> 00:15:53,620
Here.

283
00:15:54,770 --> 00:15:56,720
For real? Nice, thanks!

284
00:16:00,680 --> 00:16:03,130
Are you thinking about Enocchi?

285
00:16:04,870 --> 00:16:07,730
Is that why you've been 
avoiding me recently?

286
00:16:07,730 --> 00:16:10,360
'Cause you don't want Enocchi 
to take it wrong?

287
00:16:10,590 --> 00:16:12,170
That's not why at all.

288
00:16:12,170 --> 00:16:13,000
Then why is it?

289
00:16:14,040 --> 00:16:15,360
Why...?

290
00:16:16,250 --> 00:16:18,840
<i>It's actually because I'm 
starting to see you as a girl,</i>

291
00:16:18,840 --> 00:16:21,320
<i>and you're making my heart 
beat so fast I could die.</i>

292
00:16:21,720 --> 00:16:22,790
<i>Like I could say that!</i>

293
00:16:24,030 --> 00:16:25,540
I'm not avoiding you.

294
00:16:26,040 --> 00:16:27,590
And Enomoto-san has nothing to do with it.

295
00:16:33,440 --> 00:16:36,230
Bwa-ha! That's some good tea.

296
00:16:36,680 --> 00:16:38,480
Seriously? What was that for?

297
00:16:40,200 --> 00:16:43,480
I figured I'd test your love for Enocchi.

298
00:16:43,480 --> 00:16:45,640
That doesn't make any sense.

299
00:16:46,210 --> 00:16:48,860
I'll go buy you some tea 
from the vending machine.

300
00:16:49,650 --> 00:16:51,600
That's fine, I'll go myself.

301
00:16:51,600 --> 00:16:53,190
Watch my stuff for me.

302
00:16:55,030 --> 00:17:00,000
<i>I have no clue what my best friend's 
thinking and it's driving me nuts.</i>

303
00:17:02,900 --> 00:17:06,830
I can't believe how much guys change 
when they fall in love.

304
00:17:07,730 --> 00:17:10,830
<i>Someone once told me that girls 
and guys can't stay friends</i>

305
00:17:10,830 --> 00:17:13,460
<i>when one of them falls in love 
with someone else.</i>

306
00:17:15,560 --> 00:17:16,740
<i>Can't be helped.</i>

307
00:17:17,240 --> 00:17:19,500
<i>Enocchi's cuter than me.</i>

308
00:17:19,720 --> 00:17:22,250
<i>I know I'm super pretty too, but...</i>

309
00:17:22,890 --> 00:17:24,160
Let me be very clear.

310
00:17:24,520 --> 00:17:29,360
If you really wanted Natsu for yourself, 
you should have taken him to Tokyo.

311
00:17:29,990 --> 00:17:36,460
Natsu was prepared to leave 
everything for you and you weren't.

312
00:17:36,470 --> 00:17:39,070
You decided not to take him 
while you had the chance.

313
00:17:39,710 --> 00:17:42,570
<i>I thought he was out of his mind back then.</i>

314
00:17:43,090 --> 00:17:44,800
<i>But I get it now.</i>

315
00:17:45,720 --> 00:17:51,000
<i>The nicer Yu treats me, the greedier I get.</i>

316
00:17:51,910 --> 00:17:56,620
<i>I can't ignore that she's 
much better for him than I am.</i>

317
00:18:06,140 --> 00:18:09,600
Sunflower Festival

318
00:18:09,700 --> 00:18:12,480
Wow! It's a giant field of sunflowers!

319
00:18:14,960 --> 00:18:16,830
Yu, keep your cool.

320
00:18:16,830 --> 00:18:18,960
We gotta pick them before we check out.

321
00:18:19,310 --> 00:18:21,790
Let's find the best ones 
before someone takes them!

322
00:18:22,050 --> 00:18:22,840
Yeah.

323
00:18:26,510 --> 00:18:31,060
<i>The sunflower has two meanings: 
sweetness and vitality of life.</i>

324
00:18:31,760 --> 00:18:36,630
<i>Araki-sensei always said balance 
is the key to picking flowers.</i>

325
00:18:39,000 --> 00:18:42,440
<i>This one's leaves are too 
crooked. It feels insincere.</i>

326
00:18:43,120 --> 00:18:44,850
<i>The flower is too big on this one.</i>

327
00:18:46,640 --> 00:18:47,860
<i>This one's perfect.</i>

328
00:18:49,550 --> 00:18:52,640
<i>I want Himari to wear my 
piece created with this flower.</i>

329
00:18:53,540 --> 00:18:56,790
<i>If I'm gonna make something better 
than my wreath in middle school,</i>

330
00:18:57,150 --> 00:18:58,140
<i>it's gotta be this one.</i>

331
00:18:58,850 --> 00:18:59,870
Find one?

332
00:19:00,180 --> 00:19:01,830
Yeah, I like this one.

333
00:19:02,320 --> 00:19:04,340
I'll still look for more, though.

334
00:19:13,640 --> 00:19:15,040
Yu, guess what?

335
00:19:21,960 --> 00:19:24,690
<i>There he goes again. 
Only thinking about flowers.</i>

336
00:19:24,960 --> 00:19:29,390
<i>Once he's in the zone, 
he can't hear anything else.</i>

337
00:19:30,880 --> 00:19:33,040
Sunflowers are so pretty, right Yu?

338
00:19:37,040 --> 00:19:39,740
We should come with Enocchi next year.

339
00:19:44,740 --> 00:19:48,370
<i>I can't believe I'm jealous of flowers.</i>

340
00:19:49,320 --> 00:19:49,960
<i>But still...</i>

341
00:19:51,770 --> 00:19:53,980
Yu, I love you.

342
00:19:54,500 --> 00:19:55,660
Stop looking at flowers.

343
00:19:55,660 --> 00:19:57,230
Have eyes only for me.

344
00:20:08,280 --> 00:20:09,630
H-Himari.

345
00:20:19,400 --> 00:20:22,070
Yu, did you just hear that?

346
00:20:23,840 --> 00:20:27,160
Did you try to "Bwa-ha!" me just now?

347
00:20:27,160 --> 00:20:28,200
Stop that, will ya?

348
00:20:29,830 --> 00:20:33,050
This is serious! We have to 
look for a sunflower.

349
00:20:33,390 --> 00:20:35,670
It's not the right time to mess around.

350
00:20:38,500 --> 00:20:39,480
<i>Are you serious?</i>

351
00:20:39,970 --> 00:20:41,680
<i>This can't be real.</i>

352
00:20:42,660 --> 00:20:43,770
Hey, Himari!

353
00:20:45,210 --> 00:20:46,920
<i>Is this how it's meant to be?</i>

354
00:20:46,920 --> 00:20:48,930
<i>Even when I'm being honest,</i>

355
00:20:48,930 --> 00:20:51,250
<i>my feelings can't reach him?</i>

356
00:20:52,360 --> 00:20:54,140
Wait up! Himari!

357
00:20:54,140 --> 00:20:56,720
<i>Then what am I working so hard for?</i>

358
00:20:57,150 --> 00:20:59,650
<i>What meaning does my life have?</i>

359
00:21:01,560 --> 00:21:03,510
<i>I hate it all.</i>

360
00:21:03,510 --> 00:21:05,370
<i>I hate myself for being this way.</i>

361
00:21:05,370 --> 00:21:07,380
<i>I hate Yu for not liking me back.</i>

362
00:21:08,870 --> 00:21:10,690
Himari! Where are you?

363
00:21:12,400 --> 00:21:13,380
Right here.

364
00:21:15,130 --> 00:21:18,120
<i>There's no way he can hear me 
whispering like that.</i>

365
00:21:19,340 --> 00:21:22,740
<i>Even if the world ended 
and we were the only ones left.</i>

366
00:21:23,710 --> 00:21:28,370
<i>My voice or feelings won't ever reach him.</i>

367
00:21:31,160 --> 00:21:32,320
Himari. There you are!

368
00:21:35,460 --> 00:21:37,400
What's up with you?

369
00:21:37,710 --> 00:21:39,740
You've been acting weird all day.

370
00:21:42,580 --> 00:21:44,570
<i>I don't need this friendship ring anymore.</i>

371
00:21:45,320 --> 00:21:47,030
Wh-What are you...?

372
00:21:47,340 --> 00:21:48,490
<i>What am I doing, you ask?</i>

373
00:23:35,260 --> 00:23:39,980
Goodbye, Sunflower

